        "original_id": "5e9deb04-f9cf-5ce7-a01a-94a06b394f3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colin Chapman, Maurice Philippe\n- Products: Lotus 49, Lotus 19, Cosworth DFV\n- Organizations: Lotus Cars, Ford, Cosworth\n- Events: 1967 Formula One season\n- Media: 9 Days in Summer\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Chapman designed the Lotus 19 sports-racing car for Lotus, and Lotus built the car from 1960 until 1962.\n- Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman, born on 19 May 1928 and died on 16 December 1982, was an influential English automotive design engineer, inventor, and builder who founded Lotus Cars.\n- Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe designed the Lotus 49 Formula One racing car for the 1967 Formula One season.\n- In 1967, the Lotus 49 took part in nine Formula One races.\n- Ford made the promotional documentary film 9 Days in Summer about the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and the Lotus 49, and the film extensively featured the car's nine 1967 races.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
